      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is a $4\\times 2$ matrix?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- The matrix $P$ has $3$ rows and $4$ columns. So, its dimensions are $3\\times 4.$ $\\,\\times$\n\n- The matrix $Q$ has $4$ rows and $2$ columns. So, its dimensions are $4\\times 2.$ $\\,\\checkmark$\n\n- The matrix $R$ has $3$ rows and $4$ columns. So, its dimensions are $3\\times 4.$ $\\,\\times$\n\nTherefore, only $Q$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "2d60a04b-246b-5b06-bc1c-18161e6c42d3",
          ":answer-field/key": "$P = \\begin{bmatrix}1.1 & 2 & -0.1 & 4 \\\\ -0.1 & 5 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -0.1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$",
